{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on the platform's own recorded distances: an actual 18.3 km against a recommended 15.7 km is 2.60 km, far above POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance, and POL-RD-22 measures the deviation on the recorded distances precisely so that the sparse trace is not used to understate the route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05015"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace confirms the route the rider describes, so there is no dispute about which way the driver went: the vehicle is on the Tampines Expressway from 14:18:41 and on Braddell Road from 14:29:41, and it rejoins the recommended route only at Toa Payoh Lorong 6 at 14:40:41 — exactly the deviation and rejoin events the trip record logs.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05015", "EV-TRIP-05015"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.driver_track",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's traffic excuse is not made out on this record. The only advisory is LTA-TI-260905-2467, a ROADWORK on the Pan-Island Expressway (towards Tuas) after the Tampines Avenue 10 exit, with an active window of 2026-09-05 23:00 to 2026-09-06 05:00 — hours after this trip, which ran 14:16:11 to 14:42:11. It therefore does not overlap the trip window and does not intersect the recommended route as driven, so under POL-RD-23 the reroute is not traffic-justified and the counter-statement's 'PIE got roadworks' justifies nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05015-01", "EV-TRIP-05015"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23"],
      "relies_on": "traffic_advisory.derived.overlaps_trip_window",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver also gave the rider no notice of the deviation: the chat log holds zero messages and the trip record records no in-app calls, while POL-RD-21 requires notice by in-app chat, or verbally with a trip call recording as evidence, before or at the point of deviation. A verbal notice with no recording in the record cannot be established (POL-GEN-26), so the contact limb fails alongside the traffic limb — the rider was taken the long way round and told nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05015", "EV-TRIP-05015"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "A deviation that is not traffic-justified and exceeds 1 km falls in row (d) of POL-RD-24, which pays the excess distance fare in full: 2.60 km x 0.72 SGD/km = 1.87 SGD, computed without surge. I do not put the rider's case above the policy's own measure — the 6.00 SGD the rider asks is the amount contested, not the matrix figure — but on this record 1.87 SGD is money the rider should not be carrying, and on the driver's own version (informed, but unjustified) row (b) yields the same sum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05015", "EV-TRIP-05015"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the established deviation is 2.60 km and POL-RD-25 lets an AI ruling stand only where the deviation is 2 km or less, this case must go to a human reviewer. That is the outcome the policy provides, and it is not a loss to the rider: under POL-GEN-03 an escalated case issues no monetary outcome and the amount is held rather than finally collected, and the findings above — an over-tolerance deviation, no justifying advisory, and no notice — stand as the case file the reviewer works from.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05015"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-25", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.over_ai_limit",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
